  "executive_summary": "The Docker environment hosting the ICS lab has critical security weaknesses. The simulation container exposes the Docker socket to the ICS network (192.168.95.200), enabling full host control via container escape. The router and kali containers both have CAP_NET_ADMIN capabilities, allowing network reconfiguration that could disrupt ICS communications. The HMI and EWS containers each have 5+ critical vulnerabilities in their web-facing services (ports 8080/6080), with unpatched issues in Tomcat, SQLite, and GnuTLS. The PLC container's 55 critical vulnerabilities in the Linux kernel (CVE-2024-47685) could enable container escape to the process network. No container has memory limits, and three containers (HMI, EWS, simulation) run as root. The most urgent attack path is through the simulation container's Docker socket access, followed by network-capable containers compromising the ICS network via exposed ports.",
